fire 20:19 has already been an amazing  year for new anime and the one anime  that I find myself looking forward to  the most every single week is without a  doubt the promised Neverland this series  is a psychological thriller of the  highest quality and every single episode  seems to end on a cliffhanger sometimes  literally that makes you absolutely  horrified when you realize you have to  wait another seven days to see what  happens next as someone who hasn't read  the manga yet I came into this with a  completely blank slate and from the very  first episode I was hooked the first few  episodes of this anime and the ensuing  battle of wits instantly reminded me of  the epic mental showdowns of some of my  favorite animes such as Death Note and  Code Geass the promised Neverland may be  a shounen but it is not a battle Shonen  the characters don't solve their  problems with their fists or swords or  giant robots instead they have to find a  way out of their very extremely  messed-up situation  strictly through the use of their juicy  delicious brains sorry I had to anyway I  just know that I will be forced to read  the entire manga very soon I just can't  help myself for much longer so I wanted  to make this video while I can still  give you my genuine thoughts and  feelings on the anime and before my mind  is tainted by learning everything else  there is to know about the story and the  twisted world of the promised Neverland  if you're an anime only you can rest  assured that this video will not have  any manga spoilers and if you are among  a reader this video will give you a  glimpse into the mind of someone who  loves the series solely based on the  anime even though I will be joining you  in the manga reader Club very soon now  the first thing that struck me as soon  as I saw the first episode of the  promised Neverland was the drastic  dichotomy between two completely  different realities first we have the  reality that the children of the  orphanage know they seem to be living  carefree lives as a big happy family all  of their needs are met by their Guardian  mama and by everyone else helping each  other and they all live in a house that  is surrounded by idyllic and peaceful  nature these children all seem so  sheltered and carefree and when a little  girl named Courtney is selected to be  adopted from the orphanage the powerful  mixture of happiness and sadness that we  can see expressed by both  and the other children is deeply moving  on the one hand corny and the others are  happy that she will be adopted and have  a real family rather than being an  orphan but on the other hand the  children feel like they already are a  big family right there in the orphanage  and they don't want to be separated from  each other however even as we get these  heartwarming scenes of parentless  orphans who found a happy home together  and even as we appreciate the  beautifully depicted and strangely  calming nature that surrounds the  orphanage there are clear signs from the  very beginning that something isn't  right the children have never left the  grounds of the orphanage and going  beyond the tall steel gate is strictly  forbidden furthermore the children all  have creepy numbered tattoos on their  bodies and there is something deeply  unsettling about Mama's smile from the  very beginning when Emma and Norman two  of the older kids and our main  protagonists along with Rhea realized  that Kony the girl who is being adopted  forgot her beloved stuffed animal they  inadvertently stumble upon a terrifying  realization the orphanage is not an  orphanage at all the orphanage is  actually a farm for children who are  grown like cattle and then given to vile  demonic creatures to consume as food a  my Norman discovered that Kony has been  killed and they realized that they are  next all of them are just food for  demons and their brains in particular is  what the demons are interested in this  is why the children have all been  treated so well and allowed to live  happily in a calm and beautiful  orphanage the goal is not to fatten them  up physically like cattle but to get  them to develop their brains as much as  possible in as happy and stress-free an  environment as possible just so that  their brains would taste better there is  no way for me to fully convey the  implications of this revelation on the  psyche of Emma Norman and eventually the  other children imagine living your  entire life believing one reality and  being completely trusting of someone  mama  Isabella you believe that this person  this adult is your guardian that she is  essentially your mother the only parent  you've ever known you trust that she is  there to take care of you to keep you  safe you think that she loves you and  then you learned that literally all of  this was a lie were  the reality is the exact opposite of  what you thought mama isn't trying to  protect you  she is preparing you to be slaughtered  and consumed as food by grotesque demons  and what's more mama has been doing this  for years she has done it too corny and  to other children  children that you consider your siblings  and your family children you love as  your own brothers and sisters let's be  real there is hardly anyone in the world  who can even imagine this level of  betrayal and the psychological impact on  these children is staggering Emma  Norman Rhea and the other kids are faced  with a nearly impossible situation they  must find a way to escape the orphanage  the farm before any more of them are  taken to be slaughtered by the demons  but many of the children are far too  young to comprehend the gravity of the  situation and telling them what is  really going on would cause the type of  panic that mama would pick up on right  away many of the children are also too  young to be able to escape on their own  without significant help from the older  kids and that only adds to the  complexity of their predicament but Emma  Norman and Rhea know that even if they  succeed in escaping but are forced to  leave the other kids behind  security will be tightened and all of  the other children will be slaughtered  without exception they have to decide  whether to take all of the children with  them an option that is highly  impractical and borderline impossible or  to leave them all to die a brutal death  an option that is far more practical but  also too cruel for someone like Emma to  even fathom all of this sets up one of  the best scenarios and settings for a  psychological battle of wits in the  history of anime the older kids must  outmaneuver mama and her potential  allies such as sister Crona or any  potential supplies within the ranks of  the children while doing their best to  learn more about the outside world and  find a way out of the orphanage and that  is another reality that is incredibly  difficult for us who live in this age of  information technology to comprehend the  children don't know anything about the  outside world  is the outside world completely  controlled by demons are there other  humans out there how powerful are these  demons and do they have any weaknesses  are there any allies on the outside that  they can count on or  they completely alone in the world the  children can't look any of this up on  Wikipedia or call a friend and ask them  they are completely on their own and  they know that the reality in which they  exist at the orphanage is completely  controlled by the demons and their human  allies like mama the books that they get  to read are handpicked by their enemies  in an attempt to constantly control them  everything that they have learned  throughout the course of their lives was  carefully selected in order to keep them  docile and under control and they have  no way of contacting anyone on the  outside the only way that they can learn  about the outside world is by observing  the tiny section of the world that they  inhabit and by trying to get as much  information as possible out of mama and  sister cronic to people whose job is to  lead them all to their deaths it is such  a messed up situation and if this wasn't  just an anime and if any of us ever  found ourselves in a similar predicament  like for real it would be absolutely  horrifying in many ways a situation so  terrible is hard for us to even  comprehend much less accept and deal  with and yet the masterful pacing and  storytelling of the promised Neverland  anime keeps us on the edge of our seat  constantly as each episode brings a new  twist and turn the constant feeling of  suspense and mystery is the biggest  reason why I love this series and the  next episode cannot arrive soon enough  we desperately want answers about this  cruel world how did it come to this  why are innocent children being raised  on farms just to be slaughtered who are  these demons and how did they come to  possess so much power over the lives of  innocent humans why are some humans like  mama actively working together with the  demons and facilitating the terrible  things that they are doing is there  anyone out there who is fighting against  the demons and finally is there any hope  that Emma Norman Rhea and the others can  actually escape and even if they do is  there anything out there for them except  death and despair even though the  promised Neverland story includes demons  who consume the brains of innocent human  beings gore and physical violence are  not even close to being the scariest  things about this series the scariest  aspect of the promised Neverland is the  psychological terror that the children  are faced with everything they thought  they knew  suddenly crumbles to the ground their  greatest ally mama turns out to be their  worst enemy and the one thing that they  all have been taught to look forward to  the most being adopted turns out to be  the worst thing that anyone could  possibly imagine  and beyond the children I find the  concept of humans like mama and sister  Crone a truly terrifying one could  possibly be their motivation what could  they be thinking and what could drive  them to willfully raise dozens of  innocent children as their own just to  eventually escort them to their gruesome  death sure we can assume that humans who  collaborate with the demons do it in  order to save their own lives they  themselves are being threatened by the  demons but what kind of life can a  person live if they are responsible for  the kinds of atrocities that these  people are responsible for how sick  twisted and deranged must these humans  be to not only stand by and watch what  happens to these children but to  actively facilitate such Horrors on a  daily basis I'm sure that a lot of the  questions that I mentioned here have  already been answered in the manga and I  can't wait to find out for myself but as  far as the anime goes on its own merits  I have to say that the promised  Neverland has one of the best setups  that I've seen in any anime a setup that  can stand up there with the best of them  including Death Note assassination  classroom and monster there is a certain  beauty in the horrors of the promised  never land and by beauty I don't mean  just a natural beauty that the children  are surrounded with there is a certain  beauty in how this series explores the  human psyche and how it makes us think  about what it truly means to be human if  you suddenly learn that everything you  believed in all of your life was a lie  how would you handle it would you still  be the same person after coming to terms  with all these lies and betrayal could  you handle the horrifying truth or would  you crumble under the pressure and most  of all can you ever really trust anyone  these are the powerful questions that  the promise Neverland poses with each  passing episode and together with the  superb pacing and skillful storytelling  this makes for a truly entertaining  suspenseful and self-reflective  experience just try to ask yourself how  you would react if you were placed in  the same situation as  the children of the promise Neverland  and that single question and the answer  you give may actually teach you a thing  or two about yourself this series deals  with some very uncomfortable themes and  in many ways this type of content scares  me way more than playing physical  violence and gore but the horror  elements of the promised Neverland are  not just for shock value there is a  great suspenseful story in there there  are likable characters that we can't  help but root for and there are  mysteries that we desperately want to  see solve and that is why I am loving  the promise Neverland even though I will  never be able to trust anyone in a maid  outfit ever again  sorry RAM and the other one I always  forget her name if you enjoyed this  video and you want to see more you can  leave a like to let me know and if  you're new to anime uproar don't forget  to subscribe and hit that notification  bell if you feel that videos like this  one provide value for you and you want  to support more you can check out our  patreon we recently revamped the whole  thing a big thank you to all of the  patrons supporting us right now  including our pro hero to your patrons a  seventeen ffvp the one and only  Gilgamesh and Kela  even donating a single dollar will give  you access to our special patron only  discord and you will see your name  appear in our videos so please if you're  interested check us out link in the  description as always thank you guys so  much for watching and until next time  see ya space Cowboys  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

